// slack_reactions.proto — the REACTION INITIATOR's settings, which the
// Slack-reaction endpoints share. AGENT API section.
//
// WHAT IT WATCHES. Every message the watch user writes, in any channel, whose
// text carries a bound emoji's `:shortcode:`, and every bound emoji the watch
// user adds as a reaction onto any message. The daemon polls both through the
// user's `gns` (`gns slack search from:@<name>` and
// `gns slack reactions list --user <id>`), only while the settings are
// complete: a watch user, a repository, and at least one binding.
//
// WHAT FIRES. Each (channel, message, emoji) fires at most once, ever: its
// sha256 is recorded in the daemon's durable ledger BEFORE the binding's
// workspace is created. Slack gives no time for a reaction, so the first
// reactions read after the settings become complete records every bound
// reaction standing then as fired without firing it (the baseline); only a
// reaction added after it fires. A typed shortcode fires only within the
// poll's lookback window.
//
// WHAT A FIRE DOES. It creates a hidden INTAKE workspace in the settings'
// repository whose one turn reads the thread, names the task, and forks
// itself into the workspace that does the work, with the binding's flags
// (SlackReactionAction), then closes.

